Start pipa's board drivers (display presenter, GPU) after the source storage, behind XNU_PIPA_BOARD_START.

The same pattern as zzzzc-pipa-source-storage-start.patch: a strong call, compiled only when XNU_PIPA_BOARD_START
is set, which pipa_macos26_gpu_defconfig and pipa_macos26_ufs_gpu_defconfig do together with force-loading
libPipaGpu.a (devices/pipa/scripts/build-pipa-gpu.py), where pipa_board_start is defined (package/PipaBoardStart.c).
pipa_macos26_defconfig and pipa_macos26_ufs_defconfig do not set it: their kernels are unchanged by this patch.

What runs is decided at boot by the board's arguments, none of which board.toml passes:
  pipa-gop=1           GopFramebuffer's presenter on the firmware frame buffer (package/PipaGop.cpp); maps the frame
                       buffer the console already uses, writes no register
  pipa-gpu=<1..11>     the staged Adreno 650 bring-up (package/GpuProbe.cpp, its macOS build): mode 1 reads only;
                       modes 2 and up write clock, power and GPU registers and also need pipa-gpu-writes=1
Without them the call returns at once.

